Name: Flight Director (Flight)
Description: Leads the team.

Name: Booster Officer (Booster)
Description: Monitors the booster performance.

Name: Command and Data Handling Officer (C&DH)
Description: Monitors the avionics and computer systems.

Name: Control Officer (Control)
Description: Manages guidance and control of the solid rocket boosters, core stage, and ICPS engine from liftoff through the TLI burn.

Name: Emergency, Environmental, and Consumables Officer (EECOM)
Description: Monitors environmental control and life support systems and emergency procedures.

Name: Flight Activities Officer (FAO)
Description: Coordinates the flight plan.

Name: Flight Dynamics Officer (FDO)
Description: Monitors trajectories during all phases of the mission.

Name: Flight Operations Directorate (FOD)
Description: Relays information between the flight control team and relevant managers and leaders within NASA.

Name: Ground Control Officer (GC)
Description: Is responsible for the operation of all mission control systems.

Name: Guidance, Navigation, and Control (GNC)
Description: Operates navigation and flight control software during the mission.

Name: Integrated Communications Officer (INCO)
Description: Monitors all of Orion’s communications systems.

Name: Mechanical and Power Officer (MPO)
Description: Is responsible for electrical, mechanical, structural, and landing and recovery systems.

Name: Propulsion Officer (PROP)
Description: Is responsible for the propulsion systems.

Name: Public Affairs Officer (PAO)
Description: Provides mission commentary to the public and news media.